/*****************************************************************************
    jitFalseT -- VALUE PARITY ON AN EMPTY LOOP OR BRANCH. 2026-08-05.

    THE CANDIDATE, noted during the early-return census and measured here rather
    than argued. All three of aCTionDO, aCTionIF and aCTionWhilE end with the
    same line:

        if !result  result = falseResult;

    falseResult is a pROPERTIEs node -- isCOUNT, noPrint, value 0 -- so
    INTERPRETED, a loop that never runs and a branch that takes no arm both
    yield 0 rather than null. Under jitting all three functions return at their
    `if jitting` gate, ABOVE that line, into jitEmitWHILE / jitEmitDO /
    jitEmitGIF. Whether those emitters reproduce the convention is a question
    nobody has asked, and it is VALUE parity, not shared state -- a different
    class from the frame bracket that closed on the same day.

    WHY IT IS WORTH A FIXTURE BEFORE genParse CONVERSIONS: every rule the
    planner emits is conditionals and loops, and an action whose last statement
    is a branch that took no arm is an ordinary shape, not a corner. If the two
    engines disagree about what that action is WORTH, the disagreement is silent
    -- it is a value, not a crash, and degrade count stays 0.

    THREE ROWS, each an action whose LAST statement is the construct under test,
    so the action's value IS the construct's value:
        A  a while whose condition is false at entry -- body never runs
        B  an if whose condition is false, with NO else arm
        C  a do whose body runs once and yields nothing further

    ⚠ JITTED FIRST, ORACLE LAST. Calling the action interpreted first consumes
    its isCoded state and testing() then silently routes to jitRunIfTest -- a
    different function answering a different question, at exit 0.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (standing harness rule H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitFalse);
define
    fvIn;
    fvOut;
    fvA code={
        while fvIn > 100;
            fvIn = fvIn - 1;
        };
    fvB code={
        if fvIn > 100;
            fvIn = fvIn - 1;
        };
    fvC code={
        do
            fvIn = fvIn - 1;
        while fvIn > 100;
        };
    ;

print "== A: while, condition FALSE at entry (body never runs) ==":;
fvIn = 5;
testing(fvA);

print "== B: if, condition FALSE, no else arm ==":;
fvIn = 5;
testing(fvB);

print "== C: do, body runs once, condition FALSE after ==":;
fvIn = 5;
testing(fvC);

/*  THE ORACLE, captured LAST for the ordering reason in the header. The
    action's RETURN VALUE is what is under test, so it is assigned and printed
    -- not the field the body touched.  */
fvIn = 5;
fvOut = fvA();
print "A interpreted value =" fvOut " (falseResult is 0)":;

fvIn = 5;
fvOut = fvB();
print "B interpreted value =" fvOut " (falseResult is 0)":;

fvIn = 5;
fvOut = fvC();
print "C interpreted value =" fvOut:;

print "jitFalseT SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
